<article class="env-remark" id="AB6A8B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/AB6A8B">Remark <span data-tag="AB6A8B">6.5.1.4</span>.</a> Let $f: \calX \rightarrow \calY $ be a geometric morphism of $\infty $-topoi, and let $g: Y \rightarrow Y'$ be a morphism in $\calY $. Then there is a canonical isomorphism $f^{\ast }( \pi _ n(g) ) \simeq \pi _ n(f^{\ast }(g))$ in $\Disc (\calX _{/f^{\ast } Y})$. This follows immediately from Proposition <a href="/tag/7751D7" data-tag="7751D7">5.5.6.28</a>. </p>
